+          The canvas paints the cup. The form inside it holds real, focusable HTML, so it is
+          read by screen readers, matched by find-in-page, and translated by the browser.
+          Browsers with HTML-in-Canvas support (layoutsubtree + drawElement) lay out and paint the
+          form through the canvas; others get the identical form as an overlay sharing the canvas box.
+        -->
+        <canvas id="canvas" layoutsubtree width="480" height="560">
+          <form id="cup-form" class="cup-ui" aria-labelledby="customizer-heading" autocomplete="off" novalidate>
+            <label for="cup-name" data-slot="nameLabel">Name on cup</label>
